ops: 0 = 0\n- Assignments: 1 (`const items = ...`) = 6\n\nTotal Mass: 24\n\n**Refactored Code Mass (after)**:\n```typescript\nexport function processScenario(scenario: unknown): { results: Array<{ premium: number }> } {\n  const items = (scenario as { steps: Array<{ items: Array<{ type: string }> }> }).steps[0].items;\n  if (items.length === 1) {\n    switch (items[0].type) {\n      case \"sword\":\n        return { results: [{ premium: 115 }] };\n      case \"amulet\":\n        return { results: [{ premium: 71 }] };\n    }\n  }\n  return { results: [{ premium: 5 }] };\n}\n```\nComponent Count:\n- Constants: 7 (0, 1, \"sword\", 115, \"amulet\", 71, 5) = 7\n- Bindings: 2 (scenario, items) = 2\n- Invocations: 0 = 0\n- Conditionals: 2 (`if` + `switch`) = 8\n- Loops: 0 = 0\n- Assignments: 1 (`const items = ...`) = 6\n\nTotal Mass: 23\n\n**Mass Change**: 24 → 23 (delta -1)\n\n**Refactoring Applied**:\n- Removed duplicated `items.length === 1` check by sharing it in a single `if` and branching on item type with a `switch`.\n- Kept the function name `processScenario` because it still accurately describes the entry point for both quote and claim scenarios.\n\nBenefits:\n- Eliminates conceptual duplication (Rule 3: No Duplication).\n- Slightly lowers APP mass.\n- Makes adding the next single-item type (e.g., staff) a single `case` addition.\n- All tests remain green."}],"details":{"mode":"single","agentScope":"both","projectAgentsDir":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_19-26-36_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_kimi-k2-7-no-thinking/.pi/agents","results":[{"agent":"refactor","agentSource":"project","task":"Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 3\nRecent Green phase: Added a hardcoded branch for a single amulet returning premium 71 G.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done.","exitCode":0,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"t