uce .? If base even, result .0 or .? Let's not overthink. Using integer arithmetic: ceil(a/b) for positive integers = Math.floor((a + b - 1)/b). So premium = Math.floor((totalScaled + 19) / 20). This avoids float. Great.\n\nSo quotePremium algorithm:\n- compute base = basePremium(items)\n- compute itemSurchargeScaled = for each item: if main item or component? Components cannot be cursed/enchanted. So for all items, get itemBase (need per item base). For main items, itemBase = BASE_PREMIUMS[type]. For components, itemBase = ??? The surcharge applies to item's base premium. Components base premium per component 25 or block? The item-specific modifiers only for main items likely. Components don't have cursed/enchantment. So itemSurcharge only for main items.\n- Need per-item base premium. For components, the base premium of each component is 25 (or block). But no modifiers.\n- Compute policyBase = sum itemBase.\n- itemSurchargesScaled = sum itemBase * (curse?10:0 + high?6:0) (denominator 20). Because 50%=10/20, 30%=6/20.\n- policyModifiersScaled = policyBase * (first 2 + followUp -3 + loyalty -4) (depending on step index and customer years). For step0: first only => +2. For step>=1: first + followUp => -1. Loyalty if years>=2 => -4.\n- totalScaled = policyBase*20 + itemSurchargesScaled + policyModifiersScaled + fee*100 (5*100)\n- premium = Math.floor((totalScaled + 19)/20).\n\nWait policyBase*20 accounts for base itself. Item surcharges are already scaled. Good.\n\nLet's verify cursed sword: policyBase=100, itemSurchargeScaled=100*10=1000, policyModifiersScaled=100*2=200, fee=100. total=2000+1000+200+100=3300, /20=165. Good.\nPlain sword: 2000+0+200+100=2300 ->115.\nCursed high enchant sword: base100, itemSurchargeScaled=100*(10+6)=1600, first=200, fee=100 =>2000+1600+200+100=3900/20=195. Wait integration long-standing customer second contract has cursed enchant7: base100, curse50, high30 => item subtotal 180. Policy modifiers: loyalty -20, first +10, follow-up -15 =>