iers. For unknown item type, we need throw error (test later). For now maybe ignore.\n\nLet's modify claim-office.ts. Also need update Item type and Step type to include optional fields.\n\nWe'll write:\n\ntype Item = { type: string; material?: string; enchantment?: number; cursed?: boolean };\ntype Step = { op?: string; items?: Item[]; policy?: number; incident?: Incident };\ntype Scenario = { customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: number }; steps: Step[] };\n\nBut for now focus quote.\n\nImplement baseItemPremium(item): number. For main items lookup BASE_PREMIUMS, components 25. But component block handled at group level, not per item. basePremium function groups components.\n\nLet's refactor basePremium to also return per-item base mapping? Simpler: compute policyBase by iterating items. For each item, if component, group count and track total component base per group. But per-item surcharge needs itemBase for main items. So compute itemBase = isComponent(item)?0:BASE_PREMIUMS[item.type] (assuming valid). Then sum policyBase. Also compute itemSurchargeScaled.\n\nFor components, base premium for a group with count 3 is 60 (not per item). We'll compute component base separately.\n\nImplementation:\n\nfunction baseAndSurcharges(items: Item[]): { policyBase: number; surchargeScaled: number } {\n  let policyBase = 0;\n  let surchargeScaled = 0;\n  const componentCounts: Record<string,number> = {};\n  for (const item of items) {\n    if (COMPONENT_TYPES.has(item.type)) {\n      componentCounts[item.type] = (componentCounts[item.type] || 0) + 1;\n    } else {\n      const itemBase = BASE_PREMIUMS[item.type];\n      policyBase += itemBase;\n      let rate = 0;\n      if (item.cursed) rate += 10; // 50% = 10/20\n      if ((item.enchantment ?? 0) >= 5) rate += 6; // 30% = 6/20\n      surchargeScaled += itemBase * rate;\n    }\n  }\n  for (const [type,count] of Object.entries(componentCounts)) {\n    const groupBase = count === 3 ? 60 : count * 25;\n    policyBase += groupBase;\n  }\n  return { policyBase, surchargeScaled };\n}\n\nThen quotePremium(items, customerYears, stepIndex):\n const {policyBase, surchargeScaled} = baseAndSurcharges(items);\n let policyRate = 2; // first insurance\n if (stepIndex >= 1) policyRate -= 3; // follow-up\n if (customerYears >= 2) policyRate -= 4; // loyalty\n const totalScaled = policyBase*20 + surchargeScaled + policyBase*policyRate + PROCESSING_FEE*20;\n return Math.floor((totalScaled + 19)/20);\n\nWait PROCESSING_FEE*20 = 100. Good.\n\nNeed processScenario iterate steps with customer. For quote tests we pass customer years. For now only quote. Need keep return type. We'll implement a loop over steps, for op 'quote' compute. For other ops return placeholder.\n\nLet's update.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"functions.read:73","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/claim-office.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/kimi-k2.7-code","usage":{"input":674,"output":3166,"cacheRead":49088,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":3146,"totalTokens":52928,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784921709514,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-58cf556a-a7bc-4e9b-9907-90372d68c329","responseModel":"moonshotai/kimi-k2.7-code"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"functions.read:73","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"const PROCESSING_FEE = 5;\nconst FIRST_INSURANCE_RATE = 0.1;\n\nconst BASE_PREMIUMS: Record<string, number> = {\n  sword: 100,\n  amulet: 60,\n  staff: 80,\n  potion: 40,\n};\n\nconst COMPONENT_PREMIUM = 25;\nconst COMPONENT_BLOCK_PREMIUM = 60;\nconst COMPONENT_BLOCK_SIZE = 3;\nconst COMPONENT_TYPES = new Set([\"rune\", \"moonstone\"]);\n\ntype Item = { type: string };\ntype Step = { items: Array<Item> };\ntype Scenario = { steps: Array<Step> };\n\nfunction isComponent(item: Item): boolean {\n  return COMPONENT_TYPES.has(item.type);\n}\n\nfunction basePremium(items: Array<Item>): number 