"input":62,"output":114,"cacheRead":22912,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":94,"totalTokens":23088,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784921813516,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-a5092514-5444-44be-9898-adb61e277b0b","responseModel":"moonshotai/kimi-k2.7-code"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"functions.read:18","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"const PROCESSING_FEE = 5;\nconst SCALING = 20;\nconst PROCESSING_FEE_SCALED = PROCESSING_FEE * SCALING;\n\nconst BASE_PREMIUMS: Record<string, number> = {\n  sword: 100,\n  amulet: 60,\n  staff: 80,\n  potion: 40,\n};\n\nconst COMPONENT_PREMIUM = 25;\nconst COMPONENT_BLOCK_PREMIUM = 60;\nconst COMPONENT_BLOCK_SIZE = 3;\nconst COMPONENT_TYPES = new Set([\"rune\", \"moonstone\"]);\n\nconst CURSE_RATE = 10; // 50% == 10/20\nconst HIGH_ENCHANT_RATE = 6; // 30% == 6/20\nconst FIRST_INSURANCE_RATE = 2; // 10% == 2/20\nconst FOLLOW_UP_RATE = -3; // -15% == -3/20\nconst LOYALTY_RATE = -4; // -20% == -4/20\n\ntype Item = {\n  type: string;\n  material?: string;\n  enchantment?: number;\n  cursed?: boolean;\n};\n\ntype Step = {\n  op?: string;\n  items?: Array<Item>;\n};\n\ntype Scenario = {\n  customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: number };\n  steps: Array<Step>;\n};\n\nfunction isComponent(item: Item): boolean {\n  return COMPONENT_TYPES.has(item.type);\n}\n\nfunction itemSurchargeRate(item: Item): number {\n  let rate = 0;\n  if (item.cursed) {\n    rate += CURSE_RATE;\n  }\n  if ((item.enchantment ?? 0) >= 5) {\n    rate += HIGH_ENCHANT_RATE;\n  }\n  return rate;\n}\n\nfunction calculateBaseAndSurcharges(items: Array<Item>): { policyBase: number; surchargeScaled: number } {\n  let policyBase = 0;\n  let surchargeScaled = 0;\n  const componentCounts: Record<string, number> = {};\n\n  for (const item of items) {\n    if (isComponent(item)) {\n      componentCounts[item.type] = (componentCounts[item.type] ?? 0) + 1;\n      continue;\n    }\n\n    const itemBase = BASE_PREMIUMS[item.type] ?? 0;\n    policyBase += itemBase;\n    surchargeScaled += itemBase * itemSurchargeRate(item);\n  }\n\n  for (const count of Object.values(componentCounts)) {\n    policyBase += count === COMPONENT_BLOCK_SIZE ? COMPONENT_BLOCK_PREMIUM : count * COMPONENT_PREMIUM;\n  }\n\n  return { policyBase, surchargeScaled };\n}\n\nfunction quotePremium(items: Array<Item>, customerYears: number, stepIndex: number): number {\n  const { policyBase, surchargeScaled } = calculateBaseAndSurcharges(items);\n  const policyRate =\n    FIRST_INSURANCE_RATE +\n    (stepIndex >= 1 ? FOLLOW_UP_RATE : 0) +\n    (customerYears >= 2 ? LOYALTY_RATE : 0);\n\n  const totalScaled = policyBase * (SCALING + policyRate) + surchargeScaled + PROCESSING_FEE_SCALED;\n  return Math.floor((totalScaled + SCALING - 1) / SCALING);\n}\n\nexport function processScenario(scenario: unknown): { results: Array<{ premium: number }> } {\n  const typed = scenario as Scenario;\n  const customerYears = typed.customer.yearsWithMHPCO;\n  const results: Array<{ premium: number }> = [];\n\n  for (let i = 0; i < typed.steps.length; i++) {\n    const step = typed.steps[i];\n    if (step.op === \"quote\") {\n      results.push({ premium: quotePremium(step.items ?? [], customerYears, i) });\n    }\n  }\n\n  return { results };\n}\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784921814848},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The code looks good. Need produce final report. Since we are a subagent, we should return summary to parent. Should not write experiment-done.txt; that's only at all tests implemented. This is refactor only.\n\nNeed mention that tests pass (12 passing, 23 todo). Provide mass numbers. Need include naming evaluation. Also mention no changes to tests.\n\nLet's craft final message.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"Refactoring complete. All tests remain green.\n\n## Naming Evaluation\n\n- `baseAndSurcharges` sounded like a data structure, not a calculation. Renamed to `calculateBaseAndSurcharges` so its purpose is immediately obvious.\n- `quotePremium` and `processScenario` still clearly describe what they do, so they were kept.\n- Extracted `itemSurchargeRate` to give a name to the “cursed + high-enchant” rate calculation, removing a mutable local `rate` inside the loop.\n\n## APP Mass Calculation\n\nMass was calculated with a small AST-based counter (literals, parameters/variable declarations, binary/call/unary operators, conditionals, loops, assignments).\n\n**Before refactoring:**\n- Constants: 29\n- Bindings: 34\n- Invocations: 31\n- Conditionals: 7\n- Loops: 3\n- Assignments: 9\n- **Total Mass: 222**\n\n**After refactoring:**\n- Constants: 31\n- Bindings: 35\n- Invocations: 33\n- Conditionals: 7\n- Loops: 3\n- Assignments: 7\n- **Total Mass: 217**\n\n**Mass change:** 222 → 217 (−5)\n\n## Refactoring Applied\n\n1. **Renamed** `baseAndSurcharges` → `calculateBaseAndSurcharges` (Rule 2: reveal intent).\n2. **Extracted** `itemSurchargeRate(item)` to remove the temporary `rate` variable and make the item-level modifier rule explicit (Rule 2, Rule 3: single representation of the surcharge rule).\n3. **Simplified the premium formula** in `quotePremium`:\n   - Replaced the mutable `policyRate` build-up with a single declarative expression using ternaries.\n   - Combined `policyBase * SCALING + policyBase * policyRate` into `policyBase * (SCALING + policyRate)`, removing one multiplication without losing clarity.\n4. **Kept** the scaled-integer arithmetic and rounding unchanged so all existing quotes produce identical results.\n\n## Test Results\n\n```\n✓ src/claim-office.spec.ts  (35 tests | 23 skipped)\nTest Files  1 passed (1)\nTests  12 passed | 23 todo (35)\n```\n\nNo tests were modified."}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/kimi-k2.7-code","usage":{"input":859,"output":570,"cacheRead":23040,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":78,"totalTokens":24469,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cache